<reference id="AddEditScheduleAndCalendarBACnet-5114711B" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">New (and Edit) window for schedule import</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">This window can configure a schedule and calendar. You typically leave these properties at their default values.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">New window<indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">for schedule import</indexterm></indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section ">
            <fig id="ID-fig-0000002d" class="- topic/fig "><title class="- topic/title ">New window for importing schedules and calendars</title><image placement="break" scale="65" href="../graphic/ClientBacnetScheduleImportAddDialog_0000044854.png" class="- topic/image "/></fig>
            <p class="- topic/p ">This window opens when you expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetNetwork</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetDevice</uicontrol></menucascade>, double-click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Schedules</uicontrol> and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">New</uicontrol> or select a row and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Edit</uicontrol> in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Bacnet Schedule Import Manager</wintitle>.</p>
